                <pb facs="0798" n="778" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg778"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Lord Lyons.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-11-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 16, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Lord Lyons:</hi> Your letters of the
                    respective dates of’the 12th and 13th instant, apprising me of the prompt
                    proceedings of his excellency Viscount Monck in regard to the Georgiana, were
                    duly and thankfully received. Believe me to be, my dear Lord Lyons, always and
                    faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lord Lyons,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
